        "answer": {
          "short": "Sample answer: $10\\,010$.",
          "worked": "Choose $10\\,010$. It has five digits, with $0$ appearing three times.\n\nIts last digit is even, so it is divisible by $2$. The difference between the alternating digit sums is $(1+0+0)-(0+1)=0$, so it is divisible by $11$. Its last two digits form $10$, which is not divisible by $4$.",
